1. Free personal use
You may download, install, and run XON Shader free of charge for your own
personal, non-commercial Minecraft: Java Edition gameplay, including playing
on multiplayer servers. You may keep private backup copies for that use.
You may adjust the shader's exposed in-game settings and configuration values
for your own installation. Except as allowed by section 3, this does not permit
changes to shader source code or bundled assets.

2. Restrictions
Except as expressly allowed by section 3 or with the copyright holder's prior
written permission, you may not modify, adapt, translate, port, or create
derivative works from the source code or bundled assets; copy or reuse any part
in another shader or project; redistribute, reupload, mirror, sublicense, sell,
or otherwise supply the pack or its components to others; or bundle the pack
in a publicly distributed modpack or other downloadable collection. Link to
the official project instead. Do not remove copyright, license, or attribution
notices. No commercial-use rights are granted by this license.

3. Contributions to the official project
You may view and study the source and create a GitHub fork of the official
repository at https://github.com/Danonymos/XON solely to prepare, test, and
submit improvements to that official repository as pull requests. For that
purpose, you may modify the source and assets, run private test builds, and
publish the source changes in your contribution fork and pull request.
Retain this license and all applicable notices, and clearly identify your
fork as an unofficial contribution fork. This exception does not permit
publishing standalone shader releases, binary downloads, competing packs,
ports, or reuse in other projects.

Submit only work you own or have permission to contribute. By submitting a
contribution, you license it under these same project terms and grant the
official project's copyright holder a non-exclusive, worldwide, perpetual,
royalty-free permission to use, modify, and distribute that contribution as
part of XON Shader. You retain copyright in your original contributions.
Submission does not guarantee acceptance or grant maintainer access.

4. Hosting
The copyright holder may publish the project through services of their choice,
including Modrinth and GitHub, and authorize those services to host and deliver
it under their applicable terms. Other users receive only the permissions
expressly stated in this license. Nothing here limits rights independently
granted by the hosting platform's applicable terms.

5. Ownership and mandatory rights
Ownership remains with the respective copyright holders. No other rights are
granted. These terms do not restrict rights that applicable law makes
non-waivable, or rights in Minecraft or third-party software that the holders
do not own.

6. Warranty and liability
To the extent permitted by applicable law, the project is provided "AS IS",
without warranties of any kind, and the copyright holders are not liable for
loss or damage arising from its use. Mandatory statutory rights remain intact.

For uses outside these permissions, obtain prior written permission through
the official repository's issue tracker or the project author's public
